WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.375
One decider per row.

2
00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:05.138
The CISO sets the access baseline
and the privilege model.

3
00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.484
The identity governance
officer tiers applications,

4
00:00:08.484 --> 00:00:12.351
decides consent above the lowest
tier, and rules on exceptions.

5
00:00:12.351 --> 00:00:15.525
Application owners decide
who gets into their apps.

6
00:00:15.525 --> 00:00:17.688
Business approvers confirm the need.

7
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:21.138
Security operations can pull
consent during an incident.

8
00:00:21.138 --> 00:00:23.237
The sponsor and CIO fund it.

9
00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:26.350
And the authorizing official
owns residual risk.

10
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:31.098
Exceptions run on a clock: six months
at most, never renewed automatically,

11
00:00:31.098 --> 00:00:36.313
and one renewed more than twice goes up
to the CISO and the authorizing official.

12
00:00:36.313 --> 00:00:39.679
The decision: any exception
that leaves a control unmet

13
00:00:39.679 --> 00:00:43.412
with nothing compensating goes
to the authorizing official.

14
00:00:43.412 --> 00:00:44.690
Now, how to run it.
